IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Misrepresentation Act 1967 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation
-- (plain-text rendering of the Singapore Statutes Online text; not the official text).
-- LAYER 1, SECTIONS 4 AND 5.  Written from the text alone; nobody's point of view.
--
-- READING A RESULT.  Every rule answers a MAYBE BOOLEAN.  JUST TRUE and JUST FALSE are answers the
-- text itself gives; NOTHING means the text does not answer on these facts and is never to be read as no.
-- Every fact is a MAYBE input: NOTHING stands for a fact that was not given.  Each branch that answers no
-- carries "FALSE-kind" and the words of the text that say it; each branch that answers NOTHING carries
-- "NOTHING-kind" and why.  (NOTES.md, "Reading a result: FALSE and NOTHING".)
--
-- Section 4 asks about the date a misrepresentation or contract of sale was MADE: dates are written
-- `Date day month year` and compared directly.  Nothing here counts a period, so the Interpretation Act's
-- time module is not used.  Section 5 (the short title) creates no rule and has no function (NOTES.md).
-- "Section 5 of the Civil Law Act 1909 in force before that date" is not among the sources: whether the
-- Act "was applicable by virtue of" it is a fact the caller states.

§ `Section 4 -- Saving for past transactions`

-- The day before which section 4 looks: "12 November 1993".
`s 4 the date 12 November 1993` MEANS Date 12 11 1993

-- src:100 | 4. Nothing in this Act applies in relation to any misrepresentation or
-- src:101 | contract of sale made before 12 November 1993 except in so far as it
-- src:102 | was applicable by virtue of section 5 of the Civil Law Act 1909 in
-- src:103 | force before that date.
@ref s 4 "made before 12 November 1993" (src:100-103)
GIVEN `the date on which it was made` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4 the date on which it was made is before 12 November 1993` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the date on which it was made`
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the date was not given
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    -- before means strictly earlier: a thing made on 12 November 1993 itself is not "before" it
    -- This is a date test: a thing made on or after that day is not made before it.  The rule below turns that into its own no (section 4 does not bar the Act).
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "made before 12 November 1993"
    WHEN JUST made THEN JUST (made LESS THAN `s 4 the date 12 November 1993`)

@ref s 4 "misrepresentation or contract of sale made before 12 November 1993" (src:100-103)
GIVEN `the date on which the misrepresentation was made` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the contract is a contract of sale` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the date on which the contract was made` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4 the misrepresentation or contract of sale was made before 12 November 1993` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 4 the date on which it was made is before 12 November 1993` `the date on which the misrepresentation was made` EQUALS JUST TRUE
           OR (`the contract is a contract of sale` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `s 4 the date on which it was made is before 12 November 1993` `the date on which the contract was made` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
        THEN JUST TRUE -- "any misrepresentation or contract of sale made before 12 November 1993"
        -- This is a date test: the misrepresentation was made on or after that day, and the contract either is not a contract of sale or was made on or after it.  The rule below turns that into its own no (section 4 does not bar the Act).
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "made before 12 November 1993"
        IF `s 4 the date on which it was made is before 12 November 1993` `the date on which the misrepresentation was made` EQUALS JUST FALSE
           AND (`the contract is a contract of sale` EQUALS JUST FALSE OR `s 4 the date on which it was made is before 12 November 1993` `the date on which the contract was made` EQUALS JUST FALSE)
        THEN JUST FALSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a fact the answer turns on was not given (an input is NOTHING), and the text decides nothing without it
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

@ref s 4 (src:100-103)
GIVEN `the date on which the misrepresentation was made` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the contract is a contract of sale` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the date on which the contract was made` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `it was applicable by virtue of section 5 of the Civil Law Act 1909 in force before that date` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4 nothing in this Act applies in relation to the misrepresentation or contract of sale` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "except in so far as it was applicable by virtue of section 5 of the Civil Law Act 1909 in force before that date" (the exception is met, so section 4 does not bar the Act; it does not itself say the Act applies)
        IF `s 4 the misrepresentation or contract of sale was made before 12 November 1993` `the date on which the misrepresentation was made` `the contract is a contract of sale` `the date on which the contract was made` EQUALS JUST TRUE
           AND `it was applicable by virtue of section 5 of the Civil Law Act 1909 in force before that date` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST FALSE
        -- the text's yes: "Nothing in this Act applies in relation to any misrepresentation or contract of sale made before 12 November 1993"
        IF `s 4 the misrepresentation or contract of sale was made before 12 November 1993` `the date on which the misrepresentation was made` `the contract is a contract of sale` `the date on which the contract was made` EQUALS JUST TRUE
           AND `it was applicable by virtue of section 5 of the Civil Law Act 1909 in force before that date` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "made before 12 November 1993" (a date the text fixes in its own words; the misrepresentation was made on or after that day, and the contract either is not a contract of sale or was made on or after it, so section 4 does not bar the Act; it does not itself say the Act applies)
        IF `s 4 the misrepresentation or contract of sale was made before 12 November 1993` `the date on which the misrepresentation was made` `the contract is a contract of sale` `the date on which the contract was made` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST FALSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a fact the answer turns on was not given (an input is NOTHING), and the text decides nothing without it
        OTHERWISE NOTHING
